  "notes": [
    {
      "row": "notes",
      "title": "What the full layers are for",
      "text": "A linear recurrence compresses the past into a fixed state, which loses the ability to look up an exact earlier token. The 16 full layers restore that: they are the only places in the model that can attend precisely to an arbitrary position.",
      "code": [
        {
          "role": "definition",
          "src": "qwen35.hf",
          "lines": [
            649,
            674
          ],
          "expect": {
            "symbol": "Qwen3_5Attention",
            "first": "class Qwen3_5Attention(nn.Module):",
            "sha": "80111420",
            "span": [
              649,
              721
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "row": "notes",
      "title": "Three hybrid strategies in this atlas",
      "text": "Gemma-4 alternates sliding (1024) and full attention — both are attention. Qwen3.8 alternates a RECURRENCE and attention. Wan and H3 have one uniform block type throughout and vary nothing by depth.",
